MTS patch: longer, configurable birth cooldown (settings
mtsBirthCooldownMinSeconds / mtsBirthCooldownMaxSeconds, game seconds;
max 0 = stock).

Stock picks a mother's cooldown after each birth from a Kumaraswamy
distribution over 0..300 s (mean ~2 min): with a 60 s game year her babies
come ~2 years apart. With max > 0 the cooldown is uniform in [min, max]
instead. It is game time (time-scale.patch), so it holds while the turn
clock is paused; wait-for-mothers.patch keeps a mom on cooldown from
getting a baby anyway.

diff --git a/server/server.cpp b/server/server.cpp
index 58c58de..1b0ace4 100644
--- a/server/server.cpp
+++ b/server/server.cpp
@@ -2161,6 +2161,24 @@ static double pickBirthCooldownSeconds() {
     
     // v is in [0..1], the value range of Kumaraswamy
 
+    // MTS patch (birth-spacing.patch): with mtsBirthCooldownMinSeconds /
+    // mtsBirthCooldownMaxSeconds > 0 the cooldown is uniform in [min, max]
+    // game seconds instead (a game year is 60 s), so a mother's babies come
+    // years apart rather than ~2 minutes apart
+    int mtsMin = 
+        SettingsManager::getIntSetting( "mtsBirthCooldownMinSeconds", 0 );
+    int mtsMax = 
+        SettingsManager::getIntSetting( "mtsBirthCooldownMaxSeconds", 0 );
+    if( mtsMax > 0 ) {
+        if( mtsMin < 0 ) {
+            mtsMin = 0;
+            }
+        if( mtsMax < mtsMin ) {
+            mtsMax = mtsMin;
+            }
+        return mtsMin + u * ( mtsMax - mtsMin );
+        }
+
     // put max at 5 minutes
     return v * 5 * 60;
     }
